/-!
# Descent of level-N integral fractions to ℚ(ζ_N)

Theorem statement: `WLight.frickeFunction_intBaseChange` (`d52e793c-6559-51ae-92d0-824809981e8a`),
by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `5184fd1f-0857-5c36-9cfe-976bd371dd69`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $N$ be a positive integer, and let $L$ assign to each $\tau$ in the upper half-plane
$\mathbb{H}$ a period pair with $\omega_1 = \tau$ and $\omega_2 = 1$. Let $W$ satisfy $W_v(\tau) =
(2\pi i)^{-2}\,\wp_{L(\tau)}\bigl((\tilde v_0\tau + \tilde v_1)/N\bigr)$ for all $v \in
(\mathbb{Z}/N)^2$ and $\tau$, where $\tilde v_k$ denotes the canonical integer representative of
$v_k$, let $\mathrm{fricke}$ satisfy $\mathrm{fricke}_v(\tau) =
-\bigl(E_4(\tau)E_6(\tau)/\Delta(\tau)\bigr)/2592 \cdot W_v(\tau)$, and let $jf(\tau) =
E_4(\tau)^3/\Delta(\tau)$. Let $G, a, b : \mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ with $G$ holomorphic (complex
$C^\infty$ in the sense of `MDifferentiable` for the model $\mathcal{I}(\mathbb{C})$), with $a$ and
$b$ in the $\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of $\mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ generated by $jf$ together with
all $\mathrm{fricke}_v$ for $v \neq 0$, with $b \neq 0$ and $G\cdot b = a$, and suppose that for
some $d$ and polynomials $p_0,\dots,p_{d-1} \in \mathbb{C}[X]$ one has $G(\tau)^d + \sum_{i<d}
p_i(jf(\tau))G(\tau)^i = 0$ for all $\tau$. Put $k_N = \mathbb{Q}\bigl(e^{2\pi i/N}\bigr) \subseteq
\mathbb{C}$. Then there are finitely many scalars $\lambda_i \in \mathbb{C}$ and functions $G_i$
with $G = \sum_i \lambda_i G_i$, each $G_i$ holomorphic, each $G_i$ of the form $G_i Q_i = P_i$ with
$P_i, Q_i$ in the $k_N$-subalgebra generated by $jf$ and the $\mathrm{fricke}_v$ ($v \neq 0$) and
$Q_i \neq 0$, and each $G_i$ satisfying a monic relation $G_i(\tau)^{d_i} + \sum_{k<d_i}
p_{i,k}(jf(\tau))G_i(\tau)^k = 0$ for all $\tau$, where every coefficient of every $p_{i,k}$ lies in
$k_N$.

This is the base-change step in the study of the field of modular functions of level $N$ and its
field of constants: an element of that field which is holomorphic on $\mathbb{H}$ and integral over
$\mathbb{C}[j]$ is exhibited as a $\mathbb{C}$-linear combination of functions of the same shape but
with coefficients in the cyclotomic field $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_N)$. It is used in the $q$-expansion
arguments for cusp forms and Fricke functions, for instance in the spanning and transport statements
for $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_N)$-rational Fricke expressions; the proof cites the modularity and orbit
packages for the Fricke functions, the existence of a holomorphic quotient under a monic relation,
and the two single-constant descent theorems for integral elements (algebraic and transcendental
constant).

